      "writtenOn": "2024-01-16T17:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e so the Smart Battery may signal an error by pulling the clock or data line low for longer than Ttimeout, as specified in the SMBus specification. \n\ni2c_read16 covers timeout cases. What we\u0027re addtionally trying to cover is the error code set in the status register. SBS_DOUBLE_CHECK_STATUS_READ is for catching errors in reading the status register itself. It\u0027s guarded by a macro because it might be redundant (and it\u0027s not clear in the spec).\n\nCan you please explain your concern differently if I\u0027m missing something?",
      "parentUuid": "c6c3e63f_b438c339",
      "revId": "bef88011276030781320a8427bc9bd9b75765504",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65f4b929_dd4bcedd",
